{
  "title": "Twenty-Two Walls Is Exact for Rooms with a Corner-Only Parity Class",
  "version": "0.1",
  "date": "2026-11-23",
  "scope": "Computer-assisted. (1) A strictly simple orthogonal lattice room with a corner-only parity class and a dark pair of distinct interior lattice points, of any classes, has at least 22 walls; the 22-wall room attains it. (2) Every 15-cell such room with fewer than 22 walls lights every pair of distinct real interior points. Includes the proper-factor branch (normalized rooms, W <= 20) for lattice pairs of any classes. Excludes BBBB rooms, non-lattice marks above 15 cells, real side lengths, and 45-degree walls.",
